":"0a62fa9b99ec2e8e77d2574ec2d976feabe09947fe37052945e6c7844c770420","event_uuid":"7898fd92-0349-4fc8-83c0-9936dd8a1de1","position":{"commit_sha":"15757bc8b4682706c80b9a23867631ce1dd4fbdf","position":"1786663703954201001-7898fd92-0349-4fc8-83c0-9936dd8a1de1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"287fe19b901643ebdeadf7628a8fa5c8c0ef35f5a6030b80e64751522c0bcd54","event_uuid":"fdbcb809-eee0-4eb3-9f43-7b6b5d6cea68","position":{"commit_sha":"3815f7bdcb1587017efd947ad26f76567c6aeefd","position":"1786664022945810001-fdbcb809-eee0-4eb3-9f43-7b6b5d6cea68"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"725fd68fef5868586da24e097e3e4086d162afef96aa311ee855f0699976c83a","event_uuid":"01a6c868-d487-4757-a8c3-ce61692b4a30","position":{"commit_sha":"bba1dfda471f928fdb4eab167f1ca261ef79a63d","position":"1786664027872909001-01a6c868-d487-4757-a8c3-ce61692b4a30"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OSS consensus audit (2026-08-13): APPROVED pattern.\n\nCPython's real subprocess tests use very short trigger timeouts (for example 0.05s/0.1s) to enter timeout paths, then a generous LONG_TIMEOUT only for cleanup/resume, avoiding a brittle upper-bound pass assertion (python/cpython@dd1194e, Lib/test/test_subprocess.py#L1150-L1160 and #L1496-L1504). urllib3 similarly uses millisecond-scale test-only pool/read/connect timeouts while keeping real socket paths (urllib3/urllib3@52dfb19, test/with_dummyserver/test_connectionpool.py#L751-L812; test/with_dummyserver/test_https.py#L592).\n\nThe proposed smaller injected stall/timeout/grace/drain values with polling, real process/socket execution, and unchanged production defaults match that practice. Tracker cross-check: suave-constant-cow requires a full throughput window and fizzy-trunk-salt requires bounded group reap/retry count; neither locks production-scale seconds into the tests. No rejection found.","timestamp":1786638519589477001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final rebar-debug repair evidence (pre-Gerrit). Problem: two individual tests used production-scale real-time values and contributed 15–25s long poles despite parallel execution. Proven mechanisms were already recorded in Phase 1: the progressing snapshot test used a 10s low-speed window with a 15s real server; the ACLI terminal-read test used a 1s per-attempt deadline plus real 2s/4s logical backoffs.\n\nHeld-out proof: /tmp/rebar_short_window_oracle.py was RED on current main for both exact nodes. The fixer was isolated from that oracle. After repair, both nodes were GREEN in 3.88s. Defect-seeded mutations independently restored the socket values to window=10/server=15 and the ACLI deadline to 1s; each returned the held-out oracle to RED for the exact expected assertion, then restoration returned GREEN.\n\nFix: the snapshot test injects a 1s window and serves above the floor for 2s through the same real loopback socket. The ACLI test installs 0.1s call/grace/drain values during fixture setup, records logical backoff [2,4] without sleeping, wraps the real parent-side Popen only to record every returned PID, retains exactly _MAX_ATTEMPTS real child sessions, and polls until all are absent. Production defaults, attempts, process-group cleanup, socket semantics, coverage, and assertions remain intact; there is no wall-clock pass threshold, skip, xfail, dependency, or runner change.\n\nReplication: the snapshot node is about 2.10s and ACLI call phase about 0.31s; both complete files pass 20 tests in 11.66s. Ruff check/format and diff-check pass. Caller/sibling scope is test-only; the production timing/config surfaces are untouched and no parity gap applies. OSS consensus references and tracker rejection cross-check remain in the ticket description/comments.","timestamp":1786649939036489001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] Final Gerrit/CI completion evidence and rebar-debug report. Problem/root cause: two reliability tests encoded production-scale real-time values—a 10s low-speed window/15s loopback server and a 1s per-attempt deadline plus real 2s/4s retry sleeps—despite contracts about throughput, retry schedule, process count, and cleanup rather than elapsed seconds. Held-out `/tmp/rebar_short_window_oracle.py` was RED on current main for both exact nodes, GREEN after repair (2 passed in 3.88s), RED again when the socket mutation restored window=10/server=15, and independently RED when the ACLI mutation restored the 1s deadline; restoration returned GREEN. Fix: real loopback traffic now runs above the floor for 2s across an injected 1s window; the ACLI test installs 0.1s call/grace/drain during fixture setup, records logical `[2,4]` without sleeping, launches exactly `_MAX_ATTEMPTS` real sessions, records each parent-side `Popen.pid`, and polls until all PIDs are absent. Production defaults are byte-unchanged. Current-main replication: held-out oracle passed; both full files passed 20 tests in 10.53s; Ruff/format, project mypy across 527 files, diff-check, and ticket resolution passed. GitHub Actions run 31752047186 (https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31752047186) completed SUCCESS at 2026-08-13T23:25:43Z with all Ubuntu/macOS cells green; Gerrit change 1748 received LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, zero unresolved comments, and is MERGED as a79ed876b00d15682f27ceedf3d072ac1a4c72f5 on origin/main. No assertion, real socket/process boundary, attempt, cleanup proof, dependency, platform, Python version, mutation, coverage, or runner was removed. OSS match: CPython dd1194e and urllib3 52dfb19 use short injected trigger windows with generous cleanup. End-to-end observation: this no-macOS-queue run took 27m46s versus 34m12s immediately before; macOS took 26m43s versus 33m10s. That 6m26s improvement is observed but not attributed solely to the ~20s of directly removed waits because suite/runtime variance remains. Siblings/parity: the scoped socket and subprocess tests were both fixed; production timing surfaces remain unchanged and no additional parallel surface is missing the rule.","timestamp":1786663615215716001}],"created_at":1786598987695913001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"52f196a9-7de9-484e-8ba3-d272053ae25d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ba7d-a412-bbc0-45cb"},{"link_uuid":"0a653072-a42c-410c-a818-afc1b75d37be","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f7af-bfed-a457-46d9"}],"description":"## Context and confirmed root cause\n\nTwo accepted reliability oracles still consume multi-second wall time per matrix cell:\n\n- `test_slow_but_progressing_remote_is_not_aborted` serves a real loopback remote for 15 seconds (15.14s in the current macOS-shaped run). The contract is that sustained bytes above the configured floor survive one complete low-speed window; production's ten-second window is not itself test behavior.\n- `test_read_retried_then_terminal` uses a one-second call timeout plus production backoff sleeps across three real child processes (~9s). The contract is exactly three attempts, the logical 2s/4s retry schedule, terminal timeout, and no surviving process group—not nine elapsed seconds.\n\nProduction defaults must remain unchanged.\n\n## OSS consensus\n\nApproved. CPython's subprocess suite uses 0.05–0.1s test trigger timeouts with generous cleanup polling/deadlines, and urllib3 uses millisecond-scale test-only network timeouts while keeping real sockets. References and the cross-ticket rejection check are recorded in the existing OSS-consensus comment. Neither suave-constant-cow nor fizzy-trunk-salt requires production-scale seconds in tests.\n\n## Plan\n\n- In `tests/unit/test_snapshot_fetch_stall_abort_12e4.py`, inject a one-second low-speed window into the slow-progress test, keep the real loopback socket and above-floor byte pacing active for more than one full configured window, and retain the semantic assertion that the failure is not a stall.\n- In `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py`, inject sub-second call/grace/drain values through the existing function/constant seams; replace real retry sleeps with a recorder that asserts the exact 2s/4s logical schedule.\n- Strengthen the read-retry sentinel so each real spawned PID is recorded and polled after terminal failure, proving no child/process group survives. Keep the production retry count and real subprocess execution.\n- Use generous cleanup polling only; add no brittle wall-clock pass threshold and change no production code/default.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Slow-progress uses a real loopback socket, transfers above the configured floor for more than one complete injected low-speed window, and is not classified as a stall.\n- [x] ACLI read retry launches exactly `_MAX_ATTEMPTS` real process sessions and observes the exact production retry schedule `[2, 4]` without sleeping it.\n- [x] Every PID launched by the ACLI read sentinel is absent after terminal failure, using polling with a generous cleanup deadline.\n- [x] Production timeout, stall, grace, drain, attempt, and backoff defaults are byte-unchanged.\n- [x] Both focused modules pass and their two target tests complete in low single-digit seconds without an absolute upper-bound assertion.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `tests/unit/test_snapshot_fetch_stall_abort_12e4.py`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py`","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_snapshot_fetch_stall_abort_12e4.py","reason":"Inject a short test-only low-speed window while preserving the real loopback throughput sentinel."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py","reason":"Inject short test-only subprocess windows, record logical backoff, and assert every spawned PID is reaped."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","f7af-bfed-a457-46d9"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"fdbcb809-eee0-4eb3-9f43-7b6b5d6cea68","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["ci","performance","tests","reliability"],"ticket_id":"039b-d179-b669-4439","ticket_type":"task","title":"Shrink test-only real-time windows in subprocess and network sentinels","verify_commands":[{"command":"pytest tests/unit/test_snapshot_fetch_stall_abort_12e4.py -q","dd_id":"AC1","dd_text":"The real slow-progress socket crosses a complete injected low-speed window without a stall classification."},{"command":"pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py -q","dd_id":"AC2","dd_text":"The real ACLI timeout sentinel preserves attempt/backoff/reap semantics."},{"command":"make lint && make typecheck","dd_id":"AC3","dd_text":"Only test code changes and static gates remain green."}]},"source_event_uuids":["89597b36-0fb0-42dc-81ff-39a001a36d0b","52f196a9-7de9-484e-8ba3-d272053ae25d","3ba1ae9d-a965-468b-a8d3-a4c005b6fc5d","3674047e-cfd1-4c5e-b229-ef3f5213c110","f797c0ca-2508-432e-9921-713ba7d4347e","a6cc7821-2e21-48c8-985b-5b60d2126e40","9ccec81c-d4d9-4d63-932b-c27964602b30","18f58f67-305b-43c2-903e-05367913da49","e9504b24-8d36-4da3-b01c-edafc1392023","dac46df1-761e-40cc-9116-2cd16d8a740a","0a653072-a42c-410c-a818-afc1b75d37be","70f550dd-3d9b-4598-a717-2a0b406087dc","7898fd92-0349-4fc8-83c0-9936dd8a1de1","fdbcb809-eee0-4eb3-9f43-7b6b5d6cea68","01a6c868-d487-4757-a8c3-ce61692b4a30"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786666591795408532,"uuid":"d47c2af9-71ce-483d-b523-9c57fa6b9916"}